Z||000003||Old Lar||08-07-2001||04:15 PM||||Bob did a 3.4 for me.  I drove Bob Brown's(?) 3800 convertible while it was at Twin Lakes and it was scarey.  Steiger was finishing up a 3800 5 speed while I was there, and it sounded fantastic.  Bob was having a "fit" cause it was going to be a standard 5 speed and was a PITA to get it all together.  He did it, painted it and it was show car quality.  The owner picked it up for a test drive, and ran it into a corn field on the test drive and Bob had to repair the front. A little quicker than expected.<P>The 3800's are a pricy swap cause of the wire harness cost.<P>The 3.4L Bob put in for me included a T440 4 speed OD automatic.  At 100 mph it is running at 2600 rpm in OD.  It is running at 2700 rpm in 3rd at 70 mph which is 500 rpm less that the T125 stock Fiero automatic in 3rd at 70.  Lots of torque, and it cruises real nice at 70-80 mph (1700-2000 rpm), getting 30+ mpg on ol' 87 octane.<P>I had the Fiero intake and valve covers put on, so it looks like a stock engine.   If you look closer and know Fieros, the transmission looks lots different. A highway cruiser that is a sleeper.||||reg||1
